Verdict
==============================================================================
PARTIAL. The top-scoring pose is 4.19 A out, but a lower-ranked pose reaches 1.78 A. The search found the right answer and the scoring function did not rank it first -- which is the well-known weakness of empirical scoring, not a setup error. Treat score-based ranking on this target with corresponding caution.

What this does and does not establish: redocking is the easiest docking problem, because the receptor is in the conformation this very ligand induced. Passing shows the mechanics are right. It does not show the setup will place a different ligand correctly -- cross-docking measures that, and it is a harder test.

